# Loge: Prolog smoke test

```elixir
root = Path.expand("..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:loge, path: Path.join(root, "loge"), override: true},
  {:loge_prolog, path: Path.join(root, "loge_prolog")},
  {:kino_loge, path: Path.join(root, "kino_loge")}
])
```

## Solving

Expected: **true**, a table with `Z` = `ann` and `pat`.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(
  Loge.Prolog.Engines.Swipl,
  "parent(tom, bob).\nparent(tom, liz).\nparent(bob, ann).\nparent(bob, pat).\n\ngrandparent(X, Z) :- parent(X, Y), parent(Y, Z).\n",
  goal: "grandparent(tom, Z)",
  answers: 0,
  time_limit: 10
)
```

Expected: **false**, no table.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(
  Loge.Prolog.Engines.Swipl,
  "parent(tom, bob).\nparent(tom, liz).\nparent(bob, ann).\nparent(bob, pat).\n\ngrandparent(X, Z) :- parent(X, Y), parent(Y, Z).\n",
  goal: "grandparent(ann, _)",
  answers: 1,
  time_limit: 10
)
```

What the program prints is the Output tab. Expected: **true**, Output `hello, world`.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"eyJlbmdpbmUiOiJzd2lwbCIsImxhbmd1YWdlIjoicHJvbG9nIiwib3B0aW9ucyI6eyJhbnN3ZXJzIjoxLCJnb2FsIjoiZ3JlZXQod29ybGQpIiwidGltZV9saW1pdCI6MTB9LCJzb3VyY2UiOiJncmVldChOYW1lKSA6LSBmb3JtYXQoXCJoZWxsbywgfnd-blwiLCBbTmFtZV0pLlxuIiwidmFyaWFibGUiOiIifQ","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(Loge.Prolog.Engines.Swipl, "greet(Name) :- format(\"hello, ~w~n\", [Name]).\n",
  goal: "greet(world)",
  answers: 1,
  time_limit: 10
)
```

Expected: **Timeout** after two seconds.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"eyJlbmdpbmUiOiJzd2lwbCIsImxhbmd1YWdlIjoicHJvbG9nIiwib3B0aW9ucyI6eyJhbnN3ZXJzIjoxLCJnb2FsIjoibG9vcCIsInRpbWVfbGltaXQiOjJ9LCJzb3VyY2UiOiJsb29wIDotIGxvb3AuXG4iLCJ2YXJpYWJsZSI6IiJ9","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(Loge.Prolog.Engines.Swipl, "loop :- loop.\n", goal: "loop", answers: 1, time_limit: 2)
```

## Linting

Expected: under the editor, `Y` is a singleton (warning, on `Y`) and line 3 has a syntax
error; evaluating raises `Loge.Error` with the syntax error.

